   ],
   "design": "Test scores come from the method software into the pupil record, the group plan is a view on the support plans, and the record keeps legal deadlines as timers and flags missing items. Parents sign forms in the parent app. Report card comments start from a draft built from the teacher's own notes and marks, where each sentence cites its source; the teacher rewrites every comment and releases the card. Daily notes, the support plan evaluation and the coordinator talk stay with the teacher, and no AI sets marks.",
   "previous_blocker": "Scores, goals and deadlines were copied and tracked by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Pupil record links to method software, deadline timers, parent app signatures and comment drafts.",
   "still_hard": "Specialist reports that arrive on paper.",
   "human_edge": "Writing what a parent needs to hear about their child.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Much less copying; the teacher's judgement in the record stays.",
   "reach": [
